{
  "opening": "This release marks a significant modernization of the library, primarily by dropping support for Python 2 and introducing stricter type handling in core utilities. We are also enhancing introspection capabilities to fully support modern Python argument signatures, including keyword-only and positional-only parameters.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m02",
      "text": "The library must no longer function on Python 2 environments, raising an appropriate error or refusing import if executed under that version. The namespace helper class and the old SkipMemoization alias for SkipMemory exception must be removed from the public API."
    },
    {
      "id": "m04",
      "text": "The lzip function must accept a strict keyword argument; when True, it should raise an error if input iterables have unequal lengths. The pairwise function remains available but its behavior is unaffected by this change."
    },
    {
      "id": "m07",
      "text": "The new get_lax function must be exposed at the top level, providing a safe way to access nested dictionary values without raising KeyError on missing keys. The existing get_in and set_in functions remain unchanged in their current behavior."
    },
    {
      "id": "m13",
      "text": "The arggetter function must correctly handle keyword-only and positional-only arguments during introspection, respecting their specific binding rules. The has_1pos_and_kwonly function must accurately detect signatures containing both positional-only and keyword-only parameters."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18",
      "text": "The autocurry and rcurry functions must now support wrapping functions with keyword-only and positional-only arguments, preserving these constraints in the resulting curried callables. The get_spec function must return accurate signature information for such modern argument types."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all public names listed above are present and behave exactly as described. Verify that the removal of legacy features does not break expected imports for users migrating from older versions."
}
